From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Spatiand build <claude@prasetya.id>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Spatiand: a locked profile that was chosen asks for its lock at the start

A start naming a locked profile opens the unlocked one used last (0012): nothing opens a locked
profile by itself. But a link the wearer sends to a profile from another application (SpatiReel's
sign-in to Vibrefy, through the room's open_link) is that profile chosen, and went to somebody
else's. Such a start says so, --ask-profile-lock, and is then the named profile's, behind its PIN
window as a new window of it from the profile menu is; refused, the window closes and, with no
other, the browser goes. A SpatiMesh already running took the profile named and asked its lock
before this, and still does.
---
 chrome/browser/spatiand/profiles_sync.cc | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/chrome/browser/spatiand/profiles_sync.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/spatiand/profiles_sync.cc
@@ -264,12 +264,22 @@
   PrefService* local_state = g_browser_process->local_state();
   ProfileManager* manager = g_browser_process->profile_manager();
   const base::FilePath& user_data_dir = manager->user_data_dir();
-  // A start naming a locked profile opens the last used unlocked one, as a plain start does.
+  // A start naming a locked profile opens the last used unlocked one, as a plain start does --
+  // unless whoever started it chose that profile themselves and says so (--ask-profile-lock, as
+  // the room's open_link gives it for a link the wearer sends to a profile from another
+  // application): then the start is that profile's, behind its PIN window, as a new window of it
+  // from the profile menu is (the owner, 2026-11-24: "when open the locked profile, spatimesh
+  // should be asked the code, as like if open new window with the profile"). Its window waits in
+  // DeferShow; refused, it closes, and with no other window the browser goes.
   base::CommandLine* command_line = base::CommandLine::ForCurrentProcess();
   if (const base::FilePath named = command_line->GetSwitchValuePath(switches::kProfileDirectory);
       !named.empty() && HasLock(user_data_dir.Append(named))) {
-    LOG(WARNING) << "SpatiMesh: " << named << " has a lock; the start opens the last profile used";
-    command_line->RemoveSwitch(switches::kProfileDirectory);
+    if (command_line->HasSwitch("ask-profile-lock")) {
+      LOG(WARNING) << "SpatiMesh: " << named << " has a lock, and was chosen: its lock is asked";
+    } else {
+      LOG(WARNING) << "SpatiMesh: " << named << " has a lock; the start opens the last profile used";
+      command_line->RemoveSwitch(switches::kProfileDirectory);
+    }
   }
   std::set<base::FilePath> open;
   if (local_state->HasPrefPath(prefs::kProfilesLastActive)) {
-- 
